      "text": "To find the remainder when the sum \\(1 + 7 + 13 + 19 + \\cdots + 253 + 259\\) is divided by 6, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. **Identify the pattern of the sequence**: The sequence given is an arithmetic sequence where the first term \\(a = 1\\) and the common difference \\(d = 6\\).\n\n2. **Find the number of terms in the sequence**: The \\(n\\)-th term of an arithmetic sequence is given by:\n   \\[\n   a_n = a + (n-1)d\n   \\]\n   Setting \\(a_n = 259\\), we get:\n   \\[\n   259 = 1 + (n-1) \\cdot 6\n   \\]\n   Solving for \\(n\\):\n   \\[\n   259 = 1 + 6(n-1) \\implies 258 = 6(n-1) \\implies n-1 = 43 \\implies n = 44\n   \\]\n   So, there are 44 terms in the sequence.\n\n3. **Calculate the sum of the sequence**: The sum \\(S_n\\) of the first \\(n\\) terms of an arithmetic sequence is given by:\n   \\[\n   S_n = \\frac{n}{2} (a + l)\n   \\]\n   where \\(l\\) is the last term. Here, \\(n = 44\\), \\(a = 1\\), and \\(l = 259\\). So,\n   \\[\n   S_{44} = \\frac{44}{2} (1 + 259) = 22 \\cdot 260 = 5720\n   \\]\n   The sum of the sequence is 5720.\n\n4. **Find the remainder when 5720 is divided by 6**: We need to calculate \\(5720 \\mod 6\\). First, we find the remainder when 5720 is divided by 6:\n   \\[\n   5720 \\div 6 = 953 \\text{ remainder } 2\n   \\]\n   So, \\(5720 \\mod 6 = 2\\).\n\nTherefore, the remainder when the sum \\(1 + 7 + 13 + 19 + \\cdots + 253 + 259\\) is divided by 6 is \\(\\boxed{2}\\).",
