      "text": "To find the remainder when the sum \\(1 + 7 + 13 + 19 + \\cdots + 253 + 259\\) is divided by 6, we start by identifying the sequence. This sequence is an arithmetic sequence where the first term \\(a = 1\\) and the common difference \\(d = 6\\).\n\nThe general form of the \\(n\\)-th term of an arithmetic sequence is given by:\n\\[ a_n = a + (n-1)d \\]\nWe need to find the number of terms \\(n\\) in the sequence. The \\(n\\)-th term is 259. Setting up the equation:\n\\[ 259 = 1 + (n-1) \\cdot 6 \\]\n\\[ 259 = 1 + 6n - 6 \\]\n\\[ 259 = 6n - 5 \\]\n\\[ 264 = 6n \\]\n\\[ n = 44 \\]\nSo, there are 44 terms in the sequence.\n\nThe sum \\(S_n\\) of the first \\(n\\) terms of an arithmetic sequence is given by:\n\\[ S_n = \\frac{n}{2} (a + l) \\]\nwhere \\(l\\) is the last term. Here, \\(n = 44\\), \\(a = 1\\), and \\(l = 259\\). Plugging in these values, we get:\n\\[ S_{44} = \\frac{44}{2} (1 + 259) = 22 \\cdot 260 = 5720 \\]\n\nNext, we need to find the remainder when 5720 is divided by 6. We do this by finding the remainder of each term in the sum when divided by 6 and then finding the remainder of the sum of these remainders when divided by 6.\n\nThe remainders of the terms 1, 7, 13, 19, ..., 259 when divided by 6 are:\n\\[ 1, 1, 1, 1, \\ldots, 1 \\]\nThere are 44 terms, all of which give a remainder of 1 when divided by 6. Therefore, the remainder when 5720 is divided by 6 is the same as the remainder when \\(44 \\cdot 1 = 44\\) is divided by 6. We find:\n\\[ 44 \\div 6 = 7 \\text{ remainder } 2 \\]\nSo, the remainder when 44 is divided by 6 is 2. Therefore, the remainder when 5720 is divided by 6 is also 2.\n\nThus, the remainder when the sum \\(1 + 7 + 13 + 19 + \\cdots + 253 + 259\\) is divided by 6 is \\(\\boxed{2}\\).",
