      "text": "To find the remainder when the sum \\( 1 + 7 + 13 + 19 + \\cdots + 253 + 259 \\) is divided by 6, we first need to identify the sequence and then find the sum of this sequence.\n\n1. **Identify the Sequence:**\n   The given sequence is \\( 1, 7, 13, 19, \\ldots, 253, 259 \\). This is an arithmetic sequence where the first term \\( a = 1 \\) and the common difference \\( d = 6 \\).\n\n2. **Determine the Number of Terms:**\n   The general form of the \\( n \\)-th term of an arithmetic sequence is given by:\n   \\[\n   a_n = a + (n-1)d\n   \\]\n   Setting \\( a_n = 259 \\) to find the number of terms \\( n \\):\n   \\[\n   259 = 1 + (n-1) \\cdot 6\n   \\]\n   Solving for \\( n \\):\n   \\[\n   259 = 1 + 6(n-1)\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   259 = 1 + 6n - 6\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   259 = 6n - 5\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   264 = 6n\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   n = 44\n   \\]\n   So, there are 44 terms in the sequence.\n\n3. **Find the Sum of the Sequence:**\n   The sum \\( S_n \\) of the first \\( n \\) terms of an arithmetic sequence is given by:\n   \\[\n   S_n = \\frac{n}{2} (a + l)\n   \\]\n   where \\( l \\) is the last term. Here, \\( n = 44 \\), \\( a = 1 \\), and \\( l = 259 \\). Plugging in these values:\n   \\[\n   S_{44} = \\frac{44}{2} (1 + 259)\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   S_{44} = 22 \\cdot 260\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   S_{44} = 5720\n   \\]\n\n4. **Find the Remainder When the Sum is Divided by 6:**\n   To find the remainder when 5720 is divided by 6, we compute:\n   \\[\n   5720 \\div 6 = 953 \\text{ remainder } 2\n   \\]\n   Therefore:\n   \\[\n   5720 \\equiv 2 \\pmod{6}\n   \\]\n\nThe remainder when the sum \\( 1 + 7 + 13 + 19 + \\cdots + 253 + 259 \\) is divided by 6 is \\(\\boxed{2}\\).",
